-{"id":"INT-GATE-004","status":"pending","priority":"P2","title":"[P2] gitreins verdict-coverage audit is existence-scoped: INT-GL-3 passes ORPHAN-NOVERDICT with verdicts that graded only a pre-merge branch tip","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"40f1fa3c87c8c44285c0b64da9f7f9a6c2f74af68acfc3892ac68c473c6bdc3d"},"acceptance_criteria":"1) Reproduce the gap and state the current predicate: `python3 scripts/gitreins_verdict_audit.py .` prints RESULT: OK while INT-GL-3 sits at status=complete with commit_hash null and its only verdicts (a82440e6, cca6bf5e, ff12322b) graded f4750e9, a branch tip that is NOT the merged tree c5eb28d. expect the audit to count coverage only from a verdict whose graded commit equals the row commit or is an ancestor of the shipped tip, and to name a task whose only verdicts graded an unmerged tip. 2) Fix the predicate in scripts/gitreins_verdict_audit.py, and add the new direction to the synthetic fixture in tests/test_gitreins_verdict_audit.py: a task with one verdict on an unmerged branch tip must exit 1 naming that task id. expect the fixture to assert that arm even if the live tree is cleared by a dated exception entry, so the guard cannot silently regress to existence-only coverage. 3) Re-run `python3 scripts/gitreins_verdict_audit.py .` and `.venv/bin/pytest tests/test_gitreins_verdict_audit.py -q`; expect either ORPHAN-NOVERDICT naming INT-GL-3 or a dated exception entry for it in .gitreins/verdict_audit_exceptions.yaml, plus a green pytest run, and paste both outputs in worker_summary. 4) Do not close or re-dispatch INT-GL-3 to satisfy this row: the row is the audit's coverage semantics, and INT-GL-3's missing merged-tree verdict is the lane's own action.","reasoning":"Filed by the COS card-manager pass 2026-11-25T14:2xZ from a live run of the guard landed as INT-GATE-2 (commit 7e0304f3, verdict 2026-11-25/6ae01d07 PASS). Measured this pass: tasks_audited=225, verdicts_found=310, exceptions_skipped=2 (DEPS-005, DF-AIPP-13-R3), ORPHAN-NOVERDICT: (none), RESULT: OK — yet INT-GL-3 is a complete row with no evidence run whose verdicts were graded on branch tip f4750e9 and merged as c5eb28d, so no verdict exists for the tree that shipped. The guard therefore detects the 'complete with NO verdict anywhere' class but not the 'complete with a verdict that graded something else' class, and INT-GL-3 is the live instance. Card t_8cd14335 AC2 is the requirements-plane record; this row is the implementation delta. No worker was dispatched by the COS; one writer on the board, quiescent 4h+ at filing time.","ts":null,"created_at":"2026-11-25T14:09:59Z","attempts":0,"completed_at":null,"worktree":null,"branch":null,"sessions":null,"type":"bug","foreman_note":null,"capability_tags":[],"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-25T14:09:59Z"}
-{"id":"MON-AIPP-006","status":"pending","priority":"P3","title":"[P3] autonomy_ratio fell 0.9167 -> 0.3750 while model-dependence fell: the headline metric counts memory-navigation cycles in its denominator","detail":{"metadata":{},"fingerprint":"f9ede77584bed63419a35347e15074a18b4c7b9961b5fe2ecca9c5c11722ed12"},"acceptance_criteria":"1) Name the arithmetic from the code, not from a run: read cron_runner.py:6316-6318 and quote the assignment that computes the ratio as jev_answered divided by decisions_total in worker_summary, so a reader can see the denominator is every cycle rather than every model-consulting cycle. expect the repaired summary or a code comment to state which quantity the metric intends to measure. 2) Prove the confound from one run artifact: use cron_logs/run_df13r3r4a.jsonl as the fixture and count the cycle rows; expect 50 cycles answered by memory navigation, 30 rows with jev_answered true, and autonomy_ratio 0.3750 from the same file, which shows the nav-resolved cycles sit in the denominator. 3) Emit the disambiguating numbers: the run_autonomy block must also carry the count of cycles resolved by memory navigation and the count resolved without a teacher escalation, so a regression reader can tell fewer model calls from worse autonomy. expect those keys to appear in the summary of a fresh run. 4) Add the reader test to the default suite: run `.venv/bin/pytest tests/test_autonomy_counters.py -q` and expect exit 0 with the new assertion collected, and state in worker_summary which metric the card battle-loop autonomy bars should cite from now on.","reasoning":"Filed by the COS card-manager pass 2026-11-25T14:2xZ while judging card t_b9d5a92c AC2 ('autonomy not worse than 58/80'). Measured from the two DF-AIPP-13-R4 ledgers produced on the graded tree f0f152bb: run a = 50 memory-navigation hits, 30 jev_answered, 4 escalated, autonomy_ratio 0.3750; run b = 51 hits, 29 jev_answered, 4 escalated, 0.3625. jev_answered is exactly the set of non-nav cycles, so the ratio fell from DF-AIPP-13-R2's 0.9167 because navigation now answers half the cycles with no model call at all — the metric reads worse as the loop gets cheaper. The card-level AC was amended with that measurement and its reversal condition on the same pass; this row is the product-side fix so the next reader is not misled by the trend. No worker dispatched by the COS.","ts":null,"created_at":"2026-11-25T14:10:07Z","attempts":0,"completed_at":null,"worktree":null,"branch":null,"sessions":null,"type":"bug","foreman_note":null,"capability_tags":[],"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-11-25T14:10:07Z"}
